  "source": "Version 1 steps live-verified on 2026-11-03. Version 2 Vile Familiars NPC, objective entry/count and live kills were verified on 2026-11-04. Version 3 adds same-turn-in batch 784/837 from the hash-checked AzerothCore world snapshot; Gar'Thok identity, packed GUID and all Razor Hill/Tiragarde/quilboar walkability are explicitly pending live validation. Version 4 adds a south-side Zureetha detour sampled from verified terrain-v20 maps after live 20/8/4-yard segments hit a 17-yard wall. Version 5 adds a separately measured high-ledge recovery path after combat pulled the hunter off the normal corridor; the normal objective route remains direct. Version 6 adds a terrain-v20 low-slope Valley-to-Razor-Hill candidate corridor with four-yard-safe height deltas; the priest reached Gar'Thok and accepted 784 live, while other classes remain under validation. Version 7 adds a terrain-v20 candidate branch from the eastern Valley ledge into the Zureetha recovery corridor; the warlock traversed that branch live. Version 8 binds reward-slot maintenance at Zureetha to a live-observed vendor and measured south-side routing. Version 9 corrects that service endpoint to Duokna and reuses the complete hunter-verified western approach after the direct northern Zlagk leg hit a live 17-yard wall; the complete reward loop remains under live validation. Version 10 recommends deferring 784's Tiragarde hunt until level 6 after repeated live level-five terrain/line-of-sight stalls, without changing its server minimum level; completed objectives still turn in. RestedXP-inspired batching and ordered navigation; no third-party route data copied.",
